    board: block CF-229 on the two adapters it cannot create, and file CF-372 for them
    
    CF-229's implementation (45bd4bd) is on main and every arm I could run here is green, but
    criterion 5 says the conformance vars leg must be green "for every harness in the matrix" and the
    matrix has seven rows while only four adapters exist. deepseek:vars and pi-agent:vars therefore
    fail by name — "no adapter at scripts/harness/install-deepseek.sh" — and no change inside
    scripts/harness/*.sh can fix that, because the fix is creating two adapters that do not exist.
    
    So the row is blocked, not complete. Its note records the landed commit, the four arms I ran
    myself (vars-contract 22/0, --vars-only 6 pass 2 fail, SELFTEST: PASS, and a mutation arm that
    proved the leg goes red by name and restored the spec byte-identically), and the verdict: run
    c8018623 judged at 2e0ec0c, passed=false, INCOMPLETE on a tier-2 resource cap, with partial
    evidence that agrees with my numbers.
    
    CF-372 owns the residual: install-deepseek.sh and install-pi-agent.sh as contract-conforming
    adapters in the shape install-opencode.sh already uses (validate the contract, refuse --apply with
    a named reason rather than pretend to install something unmeasured). Both rows were already FAIL
    on check/apply/smoke before this tick, so this is an exposed gap, not a regression CF-229 created.
    
    ci=SKIP: no .github/workflows in the tree and gh run list returns [] — none configured, which is
    neither green nor a failure worth a row.
    
